<title>AUSTRALIA: NatMut says parent to get China licence.</title>
<headline>NatMut says parent to get China licence.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian life office National Mututal Holdings Ltd confirmed on Friday its parent, Axa-UAP, had been advised it would receive a licence to operate in China.  </p>
<p>National Mutual, commenting on earlier reports that a China licence would be granted, said the advice was verbal.</p>
<p>&quot;Given that the conditions attaching to this licence are not as yet known, it is not possible at this stage to say what role, if any, National Mutual Holdings or National Mutual Asia will play in that business,&quot; the company said.</p>
</text>
